# Role ACLs for the production broker. Patterns only — no credentials here.
#
# Ceiling: every enclosure shares the kms-device password, so one compromised
# device can spoof another's topics. Per-device credentials are the fix; the
# firmware reads MQTT_USERNAME/MQTT_PASSWORD from config.h, so nothing in the
# .ino changes — only provisioning.

user kms-backend
topic write device/+/access/command
topic write device/+/rack/command
topic read device/+/access/proximity_code
topic read device/+/access/event
topic read device/+/access/tamper_event
topic read device/+/rack/event
topic read device/+/power/telemetry
topic read device/+/+/heartbeat

user kms-device
topic write device/+/access/proximity_code
topic write device/+/access/event
topic write device/+/access/tamper_event
topic write device/+/power/telemetry
topic write device/+/esp32/heartbeat
topic read device/+/access/command
topic read device/+/rack/command